Note: don't create a two-handed sword or a halberd if you are equipped with a shield; this inconsistency would crash the game. If you want such a weapon, remove your shield first.~
@79298 = ~Void Weapon (Evocation)
Level: 9
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

This spell creates a planar tear in the hands of the recipient that takes the shape of a weapon that the warlord chose at the time of casting. The blade cannot leave his hand for the duration of the spell, unless replaced by another weapon shaped in the same way. This weapon made of void destroys everything that comes into contact with it. It effortlessly penetrates the strongest armor, and gives a +4 bonus to hit. It atomizes the matter around what it hits, inflicting an additional 2D6+4 points of damage. Finally it can completely disintegrate the victim it affects, if it fails a save vs. death at +4.

Note: don't create a two-handed sword or a halberd if the recipient is equipped with a shield; this inconsistency would crash the game. If you want such a weapon, remove his shield first.~
@792981 = ~Void Weapon (Evocation)
Level: 9
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 3 turns
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

This spell creates a planar tear in the hands of the recipient that takes the shape of a weapon that the warlord chose at the time of casting. The blade cannot leave his hand for the duration of the spell, unless replaced by another weapon shaped in the same way. This weapon made of void destroys everything that comes into contact with it. It effortlessly penetrates the strongest armor, and gives a +4 bonus to hit. It atomizes the matter around what it hits, inflicting an additional 2D6+4 points of damage. Finally it can completely disintegrate the victim it affects, if it fails a save vs. death at +4.

Note: don't create a two-handed sword or a halberd if you are equipped with a shield; this inconsistency would crash the game. If you want such a weapon, remove your shield first.

All allies within 5 meters of the recipient also benefit from reduced effects of the spell: the same weapon appears in their hands for 2 turns.

Note: don't create a two-handed sword or a halberd if one of the recipients is equipped with a shield; this inconsistency would crash the game. If you want such a weapon, remove his shield first.~

@793 = ~Shields of the Exalted~
@794 = ~Shields of the Exalted (Abjuration)
Level: 9
Range: 0
Duration: 2 rounds / level
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

This powerful protection spell combines three major protections.
Elemental shield gives a 40% bonus to fire, cold, acid and electricity resistance.
The physical shield grants 50% resistance to all weapon damage and a +5 bonus to AC.
Magic shield gives a 15% bonus to magic resistance, +2 to all saving throws (+4 to saving throws vs. spell) and immunity against minor spells (levels 1 and 2).
These 3 protections are inseparable and last until the duration of the spell expires.~
