They become invisible but are imperfectly covered: +3 to saving throws and 5% chance per round to be detectable, for 15 rounds.~

@797 = ~Mass Control~
@798 = ~Mass Control (Enchantment)
Level: 9
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 1 round / level
Casting Time: 9
Area of Effect: 9 m radius
Saving Throw: negates

By casting this spell, the warlord attempts to take mental control of all creatures in the targeted area. His success depends upon the saving throws of the targets: those who fail a saving throw at -6 come under his control but retain some semblance of lucidity: any violence against them by the mage or an ally breaks the spell's control and frees the creature. Those who are weak enough to fail a saving throw at -2 become puppets under his control, obeying his every command. They cannot free themselves from the grip of spell, even if orders given are opposite to their nature.
This spell can only control intelligent humanoid creatures. Orders are given by telepathy, language and cultural differences pose no obstacle.~
@7981 = ~Mass Control (Enchantment)
Level: 9
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 2 turns
Casting Time: 5
Area of Effect: 9 m radius
Saving Throw: negates

By casting this spell, the warlord attempts to take mental control of all creatures in the targeted area. His success depends upon the saving throws of the targets: those who fail a saving throw at -6 come under his control but retain some semblance of lucidity: any violence against them by the mage or an ally breaks the spell's control and frees the creature. Those who are weak enough to fail a saving throw at -2 become puppets under his control, obeying his every command. They cannot free themselves from the grip of spell, even if orders given are opposite to their nature.
This spell can only control intelligent humanoid creatures. Orders are given by telepathy, language and cultural differences pose no obstacle.~

@799 = ~Invulnerability~
@7910 = ~Invulnerability (Abjuration, Necromancy)
Level: 9
Range: caster
Duration: 5 rounds
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: caster
Saving Throw: none

Invulnerability is the ultimate protection spell, intended to make the warlord truly immortal. During the 5 rounds of the duration of the spell, the wizard is immune to all types of damage, to all effects of death, disintegration, petrification, and generally, to anything that could put an end to his life. In addition, he automatically succeeds on all saving throws.
Note: if the wizard is already affected by something harmful when casting the spell, the effect cannot kill him during these 5 rounds, but is not removed and resumes its harmful effects when the spell ends. The spell has such a power that it is impossible to keep it for long.~
@79101 = ~Invulnerability (Abjuration, Necromancy)
Level: 9
Range: visual range of the caster
Duration: 5 rounds
Casting Time: 4
Area of Effect: one creature
Saving Throw: none

As the ultimate protection spell, invulnerability aims to make the recipient truly immortal. During the 5 rounds of the duration of the spell, the recipient is immune to all types of damage, to all effects of death, disintegration, petrification, and generally, to anything that could put an end to his life. In addition, he automatically succeeds on all saving throws.
Note: if the recipient is already affected by something harmful when casting the spell, the effect cannot kill him during these 5 rounds, but is not removed and resumes its harmful effects when the spell ends. The spell has such a power that it is impossible to keep it for long.~
